#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166504 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a32afd19-5779-56f0-ad6d-1d6b541899f8" :knowledge-point/title "Understanding the Even Extension of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "b0dbd2f9-8fef-5af8-b4ce-a371e65c6441" :question/math-academy-id "e-21830" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=x^3 - x + 5\\cos x$ for $[MATH: x\\in[0,\\pi),]$ and let $f(x)$ be the **even** extension of $F(x)$ to $x \\in (-\\pi,\\pi)$. What is $f(x)$ for $x\\in(-\\pi,0)$?" :question/worked-solution "If $F(x)$ is defined on $[MATH: x\\in[0,\\pi),]$ the even extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n$[MATH: {F(x), \\mid x ∈ [0, π),; F(-x), \\mid x ∈ (- π, 0).]$\n\nIn our cases, for $x\\in(-\\pi,0)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= F(-x) \\\\\n&= (-x)^{3} - (-x) + 5\\cos (-x) \\\\\n&=-x^{3} + x + 5\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166505 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1e90af1-3fbd-5aa3-ac32-ac54c27c7224" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Cosine Coefficients From the Half-Range Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "43229a59-0b01-55ff-8b10-b1238360d277" :question/math-academy-id "e-21831" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=-6x-2$ for $[MATH: x\\in[0,\\pi).]$ Find the missing parts in the Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$.\n\n$XX_{X}^{X}$" :question/worked-solution "For our Fourier cosine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\na_n=\\frac{2}{\\pi}\\int_0^\\pi f(x)\\cos(nx)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nf(x)=-6x-2\n$$\n\nfor $x \\in (0,\\pi)$. So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\na_n = \\dfrac{2}{\\pi}\\int_0^\\pi (-6x-2) \\cos(nx)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u =-6x - 2 & ⇒u^{′} =-6 \\\\ v^{′} = \\cos (nx) & ⇒v = \\frac{1}{n}\\sin (nx)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= \\left.\\frac{2}{π}(uv\\right|_{0}^{π} - \\int_{0}^{π}vu^{′}dx) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{π}(\\frac{1}{n}[(-6x - 2)\\sin (nx)]_{0}^{π} + \\frac{6}{n}\\int_{0}^{π}\\sin (nx)dx) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{nπ}(((-6π - 2)\\sin (nπ) + 2\\sin (0)) - \\frac{6}{n}[\\cos (nx)]_{0}^{π}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{nπ}(0 - \\frac{6}{n}(\\cos (nπ) - \\cos (0))) \\\\\n&= (12(1 - \\cos (nπ)))/(n^{2}π)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since\n\n$$\n\\cos(n\\pi)=(-1)^n\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\na_n = \\dfrac{12(1-(-1)^n)}{\\pi n^2}\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier cosine series is\n\n$$\nf(x) \\sim (-2-3\\pi) + \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\dfrac{12(1-(-1)^n)}{\\pi n^2}} \\cdot \\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\cos(nx)}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166506 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96ac89a1-4179-5afe-8c1b-ebd9d47bde79" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Constant Term From the Half-Range Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "c8b4459b-e0ed-56cc-ab06-5be09baa7363" :question/math-academy-id "e-21833" :question/problem "$f(x) \\sim \\dfrac{a_0}{2} + \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty a_n \\cos(nx)$\nLet $F(x)=\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{4}\\right)$ for $[MATH: x\\in[0,\\pi).]$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for $a_0$." :question/worked-solution "For our Fourier cosine series, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\na_0=\\frac{2}{\\pi}\\int_0^\\pi f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{4}\\right)\n$$\n\nfor $x \\in (0,\\pi)$. So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{0} &= \\frac{2}{π}\\int_{0}^{π}\\sin (\\frac{3x}{4})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{π}[- \\frac{4}{3}\\cos (\\frac{3x}{4})]_{0}^{π} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{8}{3π}(\\cos (\\frac{3π}{4}) - \\cos (0)) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{8}{3π}(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - 1) \\\\\n&= 4 3 π (2 + 2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a32afd19-5779-56f0-ad6d-1d6b541899f8" :knowledge-point/title "Understanding the Even Extension of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a40b3de7-7c27-5fcd-b101-540a62c3a365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x^{2} - 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164904} {:answer/id #uuid "b5ffada9-33ba-5925-bd13-91520e7762be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} + 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164905} {:answer/id #uuid "2ff847ea-5bb3-5a94-a828-e00334ed88cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mid - x^{2} + 2x \\mid" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164906} {:answer/id #uuid "33659f3f-057f-50b5-bf51-4513b1f9cb36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x^{2} + 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164907} {:answer/id #uuid "5fc26997-85e2-5512-9d0d-6433261ec851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}x & ^{2} + 2 & x\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5ffada9-33ba-5925-bd13-91520e7762be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} + 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164905} :answer-field/id #uuid "88f2194c-5867-5f33-b139-d7b608194885" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164903}] :question/id #uuid "fcf50127-6a15-5bfa-b137-f8e9738bae25" :question/math-academy-id "q-340794" :question/problem "Let $F(x) = x^{2} - 2x$ for $[MATH: x ∈ [0, π),]$ and let $f(x)$ be the **even** extension of $F(x)$ to $x ∈ (- π, π)$. What is $f(x)$ for $x ∈ (- π, 0)$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96ac89a1-4179-5afe-8c1b-ebd9d47bde79" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Constant Term From the Half-Range Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f47c6e38-7293-5663-a864-ddaf830aea11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi^2 + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f47c6e38-7293-5663-a864-ddaf830aea11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi^2 + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232893} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f391935-24b1-5be2-9327-d8c7c663cf06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164926}] :question/id #uuid "7d95b499-c990-5e2e-96ad-0c45f0c2fce8" :question/math-academy-id "q-340814" :question/problem "$f(x)∼\\frac{a_{0}}{2} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)a_{n}\\cos (nx)$\nLet $F(x) = 3x^{2} + 2$ for $[MATH: x ∈ [0, π).]$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2π$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for $a_{0}$.$a_{0} =$ {{field-1}}"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96ac89a1-4179-5afe-8c1b-ebd9d47bde79" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Constant Term From the Half-Range Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06d43740-1c1b-503f-bc0d-76f481969199" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3/\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06d43740-1c1b-503f-bc0d-76f481969199" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3/\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232894} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab9c962d-3866-5a8a-aee0-f84a45e2caa8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164927}] :question/id #uuid "eb68e665-73e2-503c-a3f5-1fe023348ad8" :question/math-academy-id "q-340815" :question/problem "$f(x)∼\\frac{a_{0}}{2} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)a_{n}\\cos (nx)$\nLet $F(x) =-\\sin (\\frac{x}{3})$ for $[MATH: x ∈ [0, π).]$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2π$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for $a_{0}$.$a_{0} =$ {{field-1}}"}]}
